-- title:
--   Torsor isomorphism H⊗_K H≅ H⊗_k(H/K⁺H)
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a commutative ring and let $H$ be a commutative ring carrying the structure of a Hopf algebra over $k$, with comultiplication $\Delta =$ `Coalgebra.comul` and counit $\varepsilon =$ `Coalgebra.counit`. Let $K \subseteq H$ be a $k$-subalgebra, and assume that for every $x \in K$ the element $\Delta x$ of $H \otimes_k H$ lies in the $k$-submodule spanned by the pure tensors $a \otimes_k b$ with $a, b \in K$; that is, $\Delta(K)$ lands in the image of $K \otimes_k K$. Write $J$ for the ideal of $H$ generated by the set $\{x \in H : x \in K \text{ and } \varepsilon(x) = 0\}$, i.e. by the augmentation ideal $K^+ = K \cap \ker\varepsilon$ of $K$. The assertion is that there exists an isomorphism of $H$-algebras $\beta \colon H \otimes_K H \to H \otimes_k (H/J)$ (the tensor product on the left taken over the subalgebra $K$, each side an $H$-algebra through its left factor) such that for all $h_1, h_2 \in H$, $$\beta(h_1 \otimes_K h_2) = (h_1 \otimes_k \bar 1) \cdot \big(\mathrm{id}_H \otimes \pi\big)(\Delta h_2),$$ where $\pi \colon H \to H/J$ is the quotient $k$-algebra map and $\mathrm{id}_H \otimes \pi$ is the induced map $H \otimes_k H \to H \otimes_k (H/J)$; in Sweedler notation $\beta(h_1 \otimes h_2) = \sum h_1 h_{2(1)} \otimes \overline{h_{2(2)}}$. No field, finiteness, flatness or antipode-stability hypothesis on $K$ is imposed.
--
--   This is the Hopf-algebraic form of the torsor isomorphism $G \times_{G/N} G \cong G \times N$ for the quotient of $G = \operatorname{Spec} H$ by the subgroup scheme attached to the Hopf subalgebra $K$, with $N = \operatorname{Spec}(H/K^+H)$. It is used in the proof that $H$ is free over a Hopf subalgebra whose augmentation ideal is nilpotent, and in identifying the Hopf kernel of a surjection whose kernel ideal is generated by such an augmentation ideal.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_exists_algEquiv_subalgebraTensor_tensorQuotient_of_comul_mem_span.lean

